WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.885
Customers text your numbers, your agents answer from a shared inbox, and your

00:00:05.885 --> 00:00:09.121
supervisors send the same message to many people.

00:00:09.121 --> 00:00:14.242
This use case shows how the parts fit together, from the provider to a broadcast.

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:18.420
It is a recap, and it points to the videos that show each screen.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.140
This is for managers who set up two-way texting, and for the agents

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.002
and supervisors who answer.

00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:33.122
Customers who text your numbers land in a shared inbox, or with one

00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:35.210
agent, depending on the number.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:43.038
Agents claim conversations, reply, send pictures, transfer to a colleague or a queue, and close them.

00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:49.520
They also start new conversations from their own texting number, and reuse canned responses.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.330
Supervisors send the same message to many customers as a broadcast, and each

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.231
reply comes back as its own conversation.

00:00:58.231 --> 00:01:01.810
Customers who text STOP are opted out automatically.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:12.125
You need an SMS provider account, such as Twilio or Telnyx, with numbers that can text.

00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:15.150
Your administrator sets that up with IT.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:22.045
The administrator turns on SMS Messaging Channel, which turns on the messaging workspace,

00:01:22.045 --> 00:01:27.672
Contact Center Inbound Entry Points, Omnichannel Management and Content Transfer.

00:01:27.672 --> 00:01:33.040
Routed Distribution is optional, for one conversation to one available agent.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:37.962
Agents need Use the messaging workspace, and the Agent role has it.

00:01:37.962 --> 00:01:43.221
Whoever sends broadcasts and writes templates needs Send group messages and Manage the

00:01:43.221 --> 00:01:46.650
messaging workspace, and the Supervisor role has them.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:56.396
First, the administrator picks the default SMS provider and fills in its settings

00:01:56.396 --> 00:01:59.010
under Settings, Communication, SMS.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:05.419
Second, set up the contact type and import your list under Content, Import.

00:02:05.419 --> 00:02:09.960
Contacts who should not get texts can be marked Do not SMS.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:16.218
Third, add each number under Omnichannel Addresses with Text messages ticked, pick its

00:02:16.218 --> 00:02:19.930
provider, and pick the agents who text from this number.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.760
Fourth, add a Text messages entry point for each number.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.169
Send its texts to a queue or to one agent, choose shared pool

00:02:29.169 --> 00:02:34.500
or routed distribution, and write the auto-reply and the closed auto-reply.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.430
Write templates, which are canned responses, under Messaging, Templates.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:53.760
Agents filter, claim, reply, transfer, close and reopen conversations, and start new ones, under Messaging, Inbox.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:03:00.080
Supervisors send one message to many contacts under Messaging, Broadcasts.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.163
Text one of your numbers from a mobile phone.

00:03:07.163 --> 00:03:11.912
The conversation appears in the inbox, under Unassigned for a shared queue, or

00:03:11.912 --> 00:03:14.342
with the agent for a personal number.

00:03:14.342 --> 00:03:18.130
If the entry point has an auto-reply, your phone receives it.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.758
Claim the conversation, reply, and check that your phone receives the reply.

00:03:23.758 --> 00:03:28.100
Then start a new conversation to your phone from an agent's number.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.023
Text STOP from your phone and check that you receive the confirmation.

00:03:33.023 --> 00:03:34.780
Text START to opt back in.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:43.407
A number with no enabled text entry point still receives texts.

00:03:43.407 --> 00:03:45.973
They land in the unassigned inbox.

00:03:45.973 --> 00:03:51.940
With routed distribution, agents turn on the Available switch to receive conversations.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:56.454
A banner warns agents during the customer's quiet hours.

00:03:56.454 --> 00:03:58.640
It does not stop them sending.

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:05.050
A broadcast cannot be cancelled once it is queued, so send a test to yourself first.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:11.983
A provider, numbers, entry points, an inbox, templates and broadcasts:

00:04:11.983 --> 00:04:13.930
that is two-way texting.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.110
Watch the messaging videos for each screen:

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:22.043
the inbox, routing and transfers, templates and broadcasts, and setup.

00:04:22.043 --> 00:04:23.730
Thanks for watching.

